{"khaki":{"id":"706783df-9545-47e3-8534-df515b727ee8","word":"khaki","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"dust-coloured","word":"cáqui"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"dust-coloured","word":"caqui"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"glosses":["Dust-coloured; of the colour of dust."],"id":"40812b6a-90c9-430f-a3c5-d985dc220f3c"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"Khartoum":{"id":"c3570550-34de-41d0-97f8-6d2fed848cea","word":"Khartoum","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"capital of Sudan","word":"Cartum"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"But while the capture of Khartoum marks an important moment in the conflict, with the paramilitary Rapid Support Forces (RSF) deeply embedded elsewhere in Sudan and attempting to form a parallel government, analysts warn there is little likelihood of a swift resolution to the war.","ref":"2025 March 27, Nimi Princewill, “Sudan’s army has captured the capital. Is it a turning point in the devastating conflict?”, in CNN, archived from the original on 18 Jul 2025:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[25,33]],"id":"bbe5f44b-9721-4a50-b3a7-4a3959f1e37c"}],"wikidata":["Q1963"],"senseid":["en:Q1963"],"categories":["English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English proper nouns","English terms borrowed from Arabic","English terms derived from Arabic","English terms with quotations","English uncountable nouns","Entries with translation boxes","Mandarin terms with redundant transliterations","Pages with 2 entries","Pages with entries","Rhymes:English/uːm","Rhymes:English/uːm/2 syllables","Terms with Afrikaans translations","Terms with Albanian translations","Terms with Amharic translations","Terms with Arabic translations","Terms with Armenian translations","Terms with Asturian translations","Terms with Azerbaijani translations","Terms with Belarusian translations","Terms with Bengali translations","Terms