tions","Terms with Tajik translations","Terms with Tamil translations","Terms with Tatar translations","Terms with Thai translations","Terms with Tibetan translations","Terms with Turkish translations","Terms with Turkmen translations","Terms with Ukrainian translations","Terms with Urdu translations","Terms with Uyghur translations","Terms with Uzbek translations","Terms with Vietnamese translations","Terms with Welsh translations","Terms with Yiddish translations","en:Cities in Sudan","en:Khartoum","en:National capitals","en:Places in Sudan"],"links":[["capital city","capital city"],["Sudan","Sudan#English"]],"glosses":["The capital city of Sudan."],"id":"6c331f3b-2ffa-471c-89f3-73b4d390b08d"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"khan":{"id":"e6405929-6a53-4328-8019-17b74a23229d","word":"khan","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"a ruler over various Turkic and Mongol peoples in the Middle Ages","tags":["masculine"],"word":"cã"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"a ruler over various Turkic and Mongol peoples in the Middle Ages","tags":["masculine"],"word":"cão"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"categories":["English terms with historical senses"],"links":[["ruler","ruler"]],"raw_glosses":["(historical) A ruler over various Turkic and Mongol peoples in the Middle Ages."],"glosses":["A ruler over various Turkic and Mongol peoples in the Middle Ages."],"tags":["historical"],"id":"58602fee-674d-4c5f-a171-809d795ae200"},{"links":[["Ottoman","Ottoman"],["sultan","sultan"]],"glosses":["An Ottoman sultan."],"id":"b591f4ca-5efa-4649-a3c2-e69c6c458fdc"},{"links":[["noble","noble"],["rank","rank"]],"glosses":["A noble or man of rank in various Muslim countries of Central Asia, including Afghanistan."],"id":"b2986e2f-c38b-4143-9d50-9bb3319877c5"}],"related":[{"word":"khanum"}],"synonyms":[{"word":"khakan"}]},"khat":{"id":"97346857-019e-4890-8fd9-d24579d4c4d9","word":"khat","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"Catha edulis","word":"khat"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"They are chewing on khat, a small serrated, bitter leaf with remarkable stimulative properties. […] One of the great things about khat[…] is that after a good chew you need to do something—walking, running, chopping wood, vigorously reciting a poem, throwing a grenade, anything that requires boldness and physical initiative.","ref":"1967 July 9, Lawrence Fellows, “East Africa Turns On With Khat”, in The New York Times, →ISSN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[20,24],[130,134]],"id":"44fd2b5b-432c-40eb-9ded-e9b851a9fbbe"},{"text":"Of course he was an amateur of quat – hashish – which delighted the cops.","ref":"1974, Lawrence Durrell, Monsieur, Faber & Faber, published 1992, page 31:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[31,35]],"id":"0b2e0e84-333f-48ff-bff9-6d9d36521a74"},{"text":"‘And skinny Arab beggars who chew qat all day long to kill their appetites and get high on the weed.’","ref":"2004, Khushwant Singh, Burial at Sea, Penguin, published 2014, page 25:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[34,37]],"id":"64fdd666-d9f5-4c1f-a16f-a55aca08a1f9"},{"text":"Habitually munching on narcotic leaves of khat, they are easy enough to spot, their gleaming Toyota four-wheel-drives slicing paths around beaten-up wheelbarrows and pushcarts.","ref":"2011 May 24, Jay Bahadur, “Somali pirate: 'We're not murderers… we just attack ships'”, in the Guardian:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[42,46]],"id":"1a255a72-a0e8-46cb-9e43-89c997121dff"}],"links":[["shrub","shrub"],["Catha edulis","Catha edulis#Translingual"],["leaves","leaf"],["mild","mild"],["stimulant","stimulant"],["chew","chew"],["brew","brew"],["tea","tea"],["drug","drug"],["produce","produce"],["plant","plant"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"Bushman's tea"},{"word":"miraa"}],"categories":["English countable nouns","English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English nouns","English terms borrowed from Arabic","English terms derived from Arabic","English terms derived from the Arabic root ق ط ع","English terms with homophones","English terms with quotations","English uncountable nouns","Entries with translation boxes","Pages with 13 entries","Pages with entries","Quotation templates to be cleaned","Rhymes:English/æt","Rhymes:English/æt/1 syllable","Rhymes:English/ɑːt","Rhymes:English/ɑːt/1 syllable","Terms with Afrikaans translations","Terms with Amharic translations","Terms with Arabic translations","Terms with Czech translations","Terms with Danish translations","Terms with Dutch translations","Terms with Esperanto translations","Terms with Estonian translations","Terms with Finnish translations","Terms with French translations","Terms with Galician translations","Terms with Georgian translations","Terms with German translations","Terms with Hebrew translations","Terms with Hungarian translations","Terms with Icelandic translations","Terms with Indonesian translations","Terms with Irish translations","Terms with Japanese translations","Terms with Javanese translations","Terms with Korean translations","Terms with Latvian translations","Terms with Lithuanian translations","Terms with Malay translations","Terms with Mandarin translations","Terms with Norwegian translations","Terms with Pashto translations","Terms with Persian translations","Terms with Polish translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Russian translations","Terms with Sinhalese translations","Terms with Somali translations","Terms with Swahili translations","Terms with Swedish translations","Terms with Thai translations","Terms with Turkish translations","Terms with Ukrainian translations","Terms with Urdu translations","Terms with Vietnamese translations","Terms with Zulu translations","en:Recreational drugs","en:Staff vine family plants"],"glosses":["A shrub, Catha edulis, whose leaves are used as a mild stimulant when chewed or brewed as tea; also a drug