ation","bold_text_offsets":[[10,17]],"id":"be919613-749d-4bed-9be7-bfb5504855de"}],"links":[["dagger","dagger"],["Arabian","Arabian"],["countries","country"]],"categories":["Bengali terms with non-redundant manual transliterations","English countable nouns","English doublets","English entries with etymology texts","English entries with etymology trees","English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English nouns","English terms borrowed from Arabic","English terms derived from Arabic","English terms derived from Classical Persian","English terms derived from Middle Persian","English terms with quotations","Entries with translation boxes","Middle Persian term requests","Pages using etymon with no ID","Pages with 3 entries","Pages with entries","Pages with etymology trees","Quotation templates to be cleaned","Terms with Arabic translations","Terms with Armenian translations","Terms with Azerbaijani translations","Terms with Belarusian translations","Terms with Bengali translations","Terms with Bulgarian translations","Terms with Central Kurdish translations","Terms with Crimean Tatar translations","Terms with Czech translations","Terms with Egyptian Arabic translations","Terms with Finnish translations","Terms with French translations","Terms with Georgian translations","Terms with German translations","Terms with Hijazi Arabic translations","Terms with Hindi translations","Terms with Hungarian translations","Terms with Indonesian translations","Terms with Italian translations","Terms with Kalmyk translations","Terms with Kazakh translations","Terms with Kyrgyz translations","Terms with Lithuanian translations","Terms with Macedonian translations","Terms with Malay translations","Terms with Nepali translations","Terms with Northern Kurdish translations","Terms with Ottoman Turkish translations","Terms with Pashto translations","Terms with Persian translations","Terms with Polish translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Russian translations","Terms with Serbo-Croatian translations","Terms with Slovak translations","Terms with Spanish translations","Terms with Tajik translations","Terms with Tatar translations","Terms with Turkish translations","Terms with Turkmen translations","Terms with Ukrainian translations","Terms with Urdu translations","Terms with Uyghur translations","Terms with Uzbek translations","Urdu terms with redundant transliterations","en:Weapons"],"glosses":["A kind of dagger used in certain Arabian countries."],"id":"21cc351a-2b72-4137-af60-013f67dd609b"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"khagan":{"id":"d449a405-a9ed-42ea-8032-84ae10cec14a","word":"khagan","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"title of imperial rank","tags":["masculine"],"word":"khagan"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"As early as the year 740 A.D., one of the Khazar kaghans had turned to Constantinople for a missionary versed in Christian law.","ref":"1988, Milorad Pavić, translated by Christina Pribićević-Zorić, Dictionary of the Khazars, Vintage, published 1989, page 69:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[49,56]],"id":"b20d7f09-8606-4af8-bf52-029e7eb9b941"},{"text":"\"A kagan is the father, the mother and the lover of all his people. Nobody would lift a hand against him,\" said Hanukkah.","ref":"2007, Michael Chabon, Gentlemen of the Road, Sceptre, published 2008, page 52:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[3,8]],"id":"703dfcb5-86ad-45cf-a382-a6982cce34fa"}],"categories":["English countable nouns","English doublets","English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English nouns","English terms derived from Old Turkic","English terms with historical senses","English terms with quotations","Entries with translation boxes","Mandarin terms with redundant transliterations","Old Turkic terms with non-redundant manual transliterations","Pages with 2 entries","Pages with entries","Quotation templates to be cleaned","Terms with Arabic translations","Terms with Armenian translations","Terms with Azerbaijani translations","Terms with Bactrian translations","Terms with Bengali translations","Terms with Bulgarian translations","Terms with Catalan translations","Terms with Czech translations","Terms with Dutch translations","Terms with Finnish translations","Terms with French translations","Terms with German translations","Terms with Hindi translations","Terms with Hungarian translations","Terms with Japanese translations","Terms with Kazakh translations","Terms with Mandarin translations","Terms with Mongolian translations","Terms with Old Turkic translations","Terms with Ottoman Turkish translations","Terms with Persian translations","Terms with Polish translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Punjabi translations","Terms with Russian translations","Terms with Spanish translations","Terms with Tajik translations","Terms with Turkish translations","Terms with Urdu translations","Terms with Uyghur translations","Terms with Vietnamese translations","Urdu terms with redundant transliterations","en:Heads of state","en:Monarchy","en:Occupations","en:People"],"links":[["khan","khan"],["khaganate","khaganate"],["imperial","imperial"],["Turkic","Turkic"],["Mongolian","Mongolian"],["emperor","emperor"]],"raw_glosses":["(historical) A khan of khans, a ruler of a khaganate; (the holder of) an imperial rank used among certain Turkic and Mongolian peoples, equal in status to an emperor."],"glosses":["A khan of khans, a ruler of a khaganate; (the holder of) an imperial rank used among certain Turkic and Mongolian peoples, equal in status to an emperor."],"tags":["historical"],"id":"30e54aa0-07f9-49d4-ba42-38157a518b25"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"Kharkiv":{"id":"942b8492-4340-4cb6-a26a-9b3ce4521dca","word":"Kharkiv","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"city","tags":["feminine"],"word":"Carcóvia"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"city","tags":["feminine"],"word":"Carquive"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"As a schoolboy in the Soviet Ukraine’s second largest city of Kharkiv, (it was then spelled Kharkov in line with the all-permeating ‘Russification’), I was a railway buff.","ref":"2024 September 4th, Vitali Vitaliev, “A salute to Ukraine’s ‘Second Army’”, in RAIL, number 1017, page 46:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[62,69]],"id":"f9f22fc0-f34d-47c7-b46a-ad34edee2d90"}],"topics":["cities","city","location","region"],"categories":["English terms with quotations","en:Cities in Kharkiv Oblast, Ukraine","en:Cities in Ukraine","en:Kharkiv","en:Places in Kharkiv Oblast, Ukraine","en:Places in Ukraine","en:Raion capitals of Kharkiv Oblast, Ukraine"],"links":[["industrial","industrial"],["city","city"],["Kharkiv","Kharkiv#English"],["Kharkiv","Kharkiv#English"],["Ukraine","Ukraine#English"]],"raw_glosses":["(city) An industrial city, the administrative centre of Kharkiv Raion, Kharkiv Oblast, in eastern Ukraine."],"glosses":["An industrial city, the administrative centre of Kharkiv Raion, Kharkiv Oblast, in eastern Ukraine."],"id":"cf96d416-6e0c-49e9-b423-aaaa40ebf671"},{"categories":["en:Places in Kharkiv Oblast, Ukraine","en:Places in Ukraine","en:Raions of Kharkiv Oblast, Ukraine"],"links":[["raion","raion"],["Kharkiv","Kharkiv#English"],["Ukraine","Ukraine#English"],["Kharkiv","Kharkiv#English"]],"raw_glosses":["(district) A raion of Kharkiv Oblast, in eastern Ukraine. Seat: Kharkiv."],"qualifier":"district","glosses":["A raion of Kharkiv Oblast, in eastern Ukraine. Seat: Kharkiv."],"id":"b736eb24-d878-4ad9-aa41-8c37400c4ef6"},{"examples":[{"text":"But Ukraine claimed its forces had shot down one of these drones for the first time last month near the city of Kupyansk in Kharkiv.","ref":"2022 October 17, Ivana Kottasová, “‘Kamikaze’ drones are the latest threat for Ukraine. Here’s what we know”, in CNN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[124,131]],"id":"f8cc46d9-887a-47e7-b8b6-118567252995"},{"text":"The Russian military command likely chose the seizure of Vovchansk as one of the key tactical objectives of the first phase of the offensive operation in northern Kharkiv Oblast, since Vovchansk is the largest settlement immediately on the border that would provide Russian forces a staging ground close to the Russian rear to prepare for and launch the second phase of the Russian offensive operation.","ref":"2024 May 26, “Reporting from Ukraine” (channel name), 25 May: Ukrainians NULLIFY BRAND NEW RUSSIAN ENCIRCLEMENT OPERATION | War in Ukraine Explained, via YouTube, 2:23–2:44:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[163,170]],"id":"1abe2b66-1618-46c2-8a10-3397a0c0ad15"},{"text":"We switch to the developments along the front line and, uh, the Ukrainians are reporting that the Russians do reconnaissance forces… send reconnaissance forces over the border in Chernihiv, in Sumy, as well as in Kharkiv, so basically along the whole northern border.","ref":"2025 April 23, Torsten Heinrich, “Trump wants Ukraine’s Capitulation. He won’t get it. Ukraine SITREP”, in Military & History, via YouTube, 4:21–4:37:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[213,220]],"id":"1803a929-00f8-4767-a529-df81ca791d6a"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations","en:Kharkiv Oblast, Ukraine","en:Oblasts and autonomous republics of Ukraine","en:Places in Ukraine"],"links":[["oblast","oblast"],["Ukraine","Ukraine#English"],["Kharkiv","Kharkiv#English"]],"raw_glosses":["(province) An oblast in eastern Ukraine. Seat: Kharkiv."],"qualifier":"province","glosses":["An oblast in eastern Ukraine. Seat: Kharkiv."],"id":"5627e251-10f6-452d-a49c-c65da9f9871f"},{"categories":["en:Places in Ukraine","en:Rivers in Ukraine"],"links":[["river","river"],["Ukraine","Ukraine#English"]],"raw_glosses":["(river) A river in eastern Ukraine."],"qualifier":"river","glosses":["A river in eastern Ukraine."],"id":"838054dd-7864-44a4-9d09-c581eca13d92"},{"topics":["